  "narrative": {
    "intro": "SDV Office Systems has federal contract obligations of $265M in FY2026 to date across 1,610 awards, with an average award size of $164K and year-over-year change up 20.2%. SDV Office Systems received $248M from the Department of Veterans Affairs and $16.3M from the Department of Defense in the current fiscal year to date; the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $172K and the Department of the Interior obligated $0. Historical obligations show variability: FY21 $59.7M, FY22 $123M, FY23 $62.4M, FY24 $53M, and FY25 $220M. Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing is the largest market for SDV Office Systems at $194M, followed by Showcase, Partition, Shelving, and Locker Manufacturing at $43.5M and Medical, Dental, and Hospital Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers at $16M. Other notable markets include Office Furniture (except Wood) Manufacturing at $4.9M and Electromedical and Electrotherapeutic Apparatus Manufacturing at $2.8M. These figures reflect contract obligations for the fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are SDV Office Systems' biggest buyers?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the biggest buyer, obligating $248M to SDV Office Systems in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense is the second-largest buyer with $16.3M. The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $172K and the Department of the Interior obligated $0 in the same period."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets drive SDV Office Systems' federal obligations?",
        "body": "Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing drives the largest share of obligations at $194M. Showcase, Partition, Shelving, and Locker Manufacturing contributes $43.5M and Medical, Dental, and Hospital Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers contributes $16M. Smaller markets include Office Furniture (except Wood) Manufacturing at $4.9M and Electromedical and Electrotherapeutic Apparatus Manufacturing at $2.8M."
      }
    ]
